List all Pods in a given namespace.

## Endpoint

```
GET /api/v1/namespaces/{namespace}/pods
```

## Path Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
|-----------|------|-------------|
| `namespace` | string | The namespace to list Pods from |

## Query Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
| `labelSelector` | string | No | Filter by label (e.g., `app=nginx`) |
| `fieldSelector` | string | No | Filter by field (e.g., `status.phase=Running`) |
| `limit` | integer | No | Maximum number of results to return |
| `continue` | string | No | Token for paginating large result sets |

## Response (200 OK)

```json
{
  "apiVersion": "v1",
  "kind": "PodList",
  "metadata": {
    "resourceVersion": "12345"
  },
  "items": [
    {
      "metadata": {
        "name": "nginx-pod",
        "namespace": "default",
        "labels": {"app": "nginx"}
      },
      "spec": {
        "containers": [{"name": "nginx", "image": "nginx:1.25"}]
      },
      "status": {
        "phase": "Running",
        "podIP": "10.244.0.5"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

List all Deployments in the specified namespace.

## Endpoint

```
GET /apis/apps/v1/namespaces/{namespace}/deployments
```

## Path Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
|-----------|------|-------------|
| `namespace` | string | The namespace to list Deployments from |

## Query Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
| `labelSelector` | string | No | Filter by label (e.g., `app=nginx`) |
| `limit` | integer | No | Maximum number of results |
| `continue` | string | No | Pagination continuation token |

## Response (200 OK)

```json
{
  "apiVersion": "apps/v1",
  "kind": "DeploymentList",
  "items": [
    {
      "metadata": {
        "name": "nginx-deployment",
        "namespace": "default"
      },
      "spec": {
        "replicas": 3,
        "selector": {"matchLabels": {"app": "nginx"}}
      },
      "status": {
        "readyReplicas": 3,
        "availableReplicas": 3
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

List all Namespaces in the cluster.

## Endpoint

```
GET /api/v1/namespaces
```

## Query Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
| `labelSelector` | string | No | Filter namespaces by label |
| `limit` | integer | No | Maximum number of results |

## Response (200 OK)

```json
{
  "apiVersion": "v1",
  "kind": "NamespaceList",
  "items": [
    {
      "metadata": {
        "name": "default",
        "labels": {"kubernetes.io/metadata.name": "default"}
      },
      "status": {"phase": "Active"}
    },
    {
      "metadata": {"name": "kube-system"},
      "status": {"phase": "Active"}
    },
    {
      "metadata": {"name": "kube-public"},
      "status": {"phase": "Active"}
    }
  ]
}
```

## Notes

- Namespaces are cluster-scoped resources (not namespaced themselves)
- System namespaces (`kube-system`, `kube-public`, `kube-node-lease`) are created automatically
- Namespace names must be valid DNS labels (lowercase alphanumeric and hyphens)

List all Nodes in the cluster.

## Endpoint

```
GET /api/v1/nodes
```

## Query Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
| `labelSelector` | string | No | Filter by label (e.g., `node-role.kubernetes.io/control-plane`) |
| `fieldSelector` | string | No | Filter by field (e.g., `metadata.name=node-1`) |
| `limit` | integer | No | Maximum number of results |

## Response (200 OK)

```json
{
  "apiVersion": "v1",
  "kind": "NodeList",
  "items": [
    {
      "metadata": {
        "name": "node-1",
        "labels": {
          "kubernetes.io/os": "linux",
          "node-role.kubernetes.io/control-plane": ""
        }
      },
      "status": {
        "conditions": [
          {"type": "Ready", "status": "True"}
        ],
        "capacity": {
          "cpu": "4",
          "memory": "16Gi",
          "pods": "110"
        },
        "nodeInfo": {
          "kubeletVersion": "v1.30.0",
          "containerRuntimeVersion": "containerd://1.7.2",
          "osImage": "Ubuntu 22.04.4 LTS"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Notes

- Nodes are cluster-scoped resources
- The `Ready` condition indicates whether the node is healthy and able to accept Pods
- Node capacity and allocatable resources help the scheduler make placement decisions
